---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Section } from "@/components/custom/section";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms & Conditions | ACOSA"
  description="Read the terms and conditions governing use of the ACOSA website and services."
>
  <Section>
    <article class="mx-auto flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-8">
      <header class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h1 class="type-h1">Website Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">
          Effective date: 31.10.2026 · Last updated: 03.11.2026
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">1. Introduction</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">Welcome to ACOSA.</p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          These Terms &amp; Conditions govern your use of the ACOSA website and
          its accommodation discovery, enquiry and property listing services.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          By accessing or using the website, you agree to comply with these
          Terms, subject to your rights under applicable South African law.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Please read them carefully.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">2. About ACOSA</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA is a curated business-accommodation discovery platform
          connecting prospective guests, corporate accommodation coordinators
          and other accommodation seekers with selected accommodation providers
          in South Africa.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA helps visitors discover properties and make relevant enquiries.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Unless expressly agreed otherwise in writing, ACOSA does not itself
          provide accommodation, operate the listed establishments or act as the
          contracting party for accommodation reservations.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">3. Website information</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA aims to present clear, useful and reasonably accurate
          information about listed accommodation.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Property descriptions, photographs, facilities, availability and other
          details may be supplied by accommodation providers.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Although ACOSA reviews properties against its listing criteria,
          information may change after publication.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Visitors should confirm important details directly with the
          accommodation provider before making a reservation or payment.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">4. Accommodation enquiries and reservations</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Visitors may use ACOSA to discover properties or request assistance
          identifying relevant accommodation options.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Submitting an enquiry through ACOSA does not constitute a confirmed
          reservation.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Unless ACOSA expressly communicates otherwise in writing:
        </p>
        <ul class="text-foreground/80 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 leading-relaxed">
          <li>
            Accommodation availability is confirmed by the relevant property.
          </li>
          <li>
            Accommodation rates and booking conditions are determined by the
            property.
          </li>
          <li>
            Reservations are concluded directly with the accommodation provider.
          </li>
          <li>
            Payment arrangements are agreed directly with the accommodation
            provider.
          </li>
          <li>
            Cancellation and refund conditions are determined by the relevant
            booking agreement and applicable law.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Visitors should review the accommodation provider's booking terms
          before confirming a reservation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">5. Accommodation providers</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Each accommodation provider is responsible for operating its
          establishment and delivering the accommodation services it offers.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          This includes maintaining accurate property information and complying
          with applicable legal, safety and operational requirements.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA's property review process is intended to support the relevance
          and quality of listings.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          However, inclusion on the platform does not constitute an
          unconditional guarantee of any property's facilities, service
          standards, availability or suitability for every traveller.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">6. Property listing applications</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Property owners and authorised representatives may request an
          application to list their establishment on ACOSA.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Submitting an enquiry or application does not guarantee acceptance.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA reserves the right to assess applications against its published
          or internally established listing criteria, subject to applicable law.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Additional information, supporting documents or clarification may be
          requested during the review process.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          If approved, the property owner will receive information about the
          applicable listing arrangements and onboarding requirements.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">7. Paid property listings</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA may charge fees for approved property listings and associated
          services.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Applicable pricing, payment arrangements, service periods, renewal
          conditions and cancellation terms will be communicated separately
          before a paid listing agreement is concluded.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          The commercial relationship between ACOSA and an accommodation
          provider will be governed by the applicable listing agreement and any
          additional terms expressly accepted by the parties.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          These Website Terms do not, by themselves, create a paid listing
          agreement.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">8. Listing visibility and performance</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA provides an additional channel through which accommodation
          providers may be discovered by relevant audiences.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          However, ACOSA does not guarantee:
        </p>
        <ul class="text-foreground/80 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 leading-relaxed">
          <li>A particular number of website visitors.</li>
          <li>A specific search ranking or level of exposure.</li>
          <li>A minimum number of enquiries.</li>
          <li>Confirmed accommodation reservations.</li>
          <li>Occupancy levels or revenue.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Where technically available, ACOSA may provide property owners with
          performance information such as listing views and contact-action
          activity.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Such information reflects measurable website activity and should not
          be interpreted as a guarantee of commercial results.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">9. Accuracy of submitted information</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Users and accommodation providers agree to supply information that is
          accurate and not intentionally misleading.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Property owners are responsible for notifying ACOSA of material
          changes to their establishment's details, including contact
          information, facilities, ownership or operational status.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA may request corrections or temporarily withhold information from
          publication where reasonably necessary to maintain listing accuracy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">
          10. Photographs, descriptions and intellectual property
        </h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Accommodation providers submitting photographs, descriptions, logos or
          other materials confirm that they own the relevant rights or have
          permission to supply the materials for publication.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          By submitting approved listing materials, providers grant ACOSA
          permission to use, reproduce, display and adapt those materials as
          reasonably necessary to publish and promote their listing, subject to
          any applicable written agreement.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Ownership of the original materials remains with the relevant rights
          holder.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA's own website design, branding, original copy and other
          proprietary materials may not be reproduced or commercially exploited
          without appropriate permission.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">11. Acceptable website use</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">Visitors agree not to:</p>
        <ul class="text-foreground/80 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 leading-relaxed">
          <li>Submit false or misleading information.</li>
          <li>Impersonate another person or organisation.</li>
          <li>Attempt unauthorised access to website systems.</li>
          <li>Introduce malicious software.</li>
          <li>
            Use automated tools to extract substantial website content without
            permission.
          </li>
          <li>Interfere with website security or functionality.</li>
          <li>Use the website for unlawful or fraudulent purposes.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA may take reasonable steps to protect the website and its users
          against misuse.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">12. Third-party services and external links</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          The website may include links to external property websites, messaging
          applications, maps and other third-party services.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          These services operate independently of ACOSA.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Use of third-party services may be subject to their own terms, privacy
          policies and technical limitations.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA is not responsible for independently operated third-party
          websites or services, except to the extent that responsibility arises
          under applicable law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">13. Website availability</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA aims to maintain a functional and accessible website.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          However, occasional interruptions may occur because of maintenance,
          technical issues, connectivity problems or circumstances beyond our
          reasonable control.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA may update website content and functionality as its services
          develop.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">14. Responsibility and liability</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA is responsible for its own conduct and obligations under
          applicable law.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Accommodation providers remain responsible for the accommodation
          services they supply and the contractual commitments they make to
          guests.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          To the extent permitted by applicable law, ACOSA does not assume
          responsibility for losses arising solely from the independent acts or
          omissions of accommodation providers or third-party services.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Nothing in these Terms excludes or restricts liability where doing so
          would be unlawful, or limits rights and remedies that cannot legally
          be excluded under South African consumer protection legislation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">15. Privacy</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA processes personal information in accordance with its
          <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/privacy"
            >Privacy Policy</a
          >
          and applicable South African law.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Please review the Privacy Policy for information about the collection,
          use and protection of personal information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">16. Complaints and disputes</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Visitors and accommodation providers are encouraged to contact ACOSA
          if they have concerns about website information, listing
          administration or the services provided directly by ACOSA.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Complaints relating to an accommodation stay, reservation, payment or
          cancellation should ordinarily be directed to the accommodation
          provider responsible for that transaction.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA may assist with communication where appropriate but does not
          automatically assume responsibility for resolving disputes between
          guests and independent accommodation providers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">17. Governing law</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          These Terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of South Africa.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Any dispute relating to these Terms will be dealt with in accordance
          with applicable South African law and the jurisdiction of the
          appropriate courts or other competent dispute-resolution bodies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">18. Changes to these Terms</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          ACOSA may update these Website Terms to reflect changes in its
          services, operations or legal requirements.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Updated Terms will be published on the website.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          Changes will not automatically override the terms of an existing
          separate listing agreement.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="type-h2">19. Contact information</h2>
        <address
          class="text-foreground/80 flex flex-col gap-1 leading-relaxed not-italic"
        >
          <strong>ACOSA</strong>
          <span>Registered business name: ACOSA (PTY) LTD</span>
          <span>Registration number: 2025/703956/07</span>
          <span>
            Email:
            <a
              class="underline underline-offset-4"
              href="mailto:info@acosa.co.za"
            >
              info@acosa.co.za
            </a>
          </span>
          <span>Telephone: 0766228202</span>
        </address>
      </section>
    </article>
  </Section>
</Layout>
